zilla-v1: ZillaCode problems adapted for Datapass Workbench

This pack contains material adapted from ZillaCode (https://github.com/davidzajac1/zillacode), an open-source
collection of data engineering practice problems by David Zajac and contributors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE in this folder).

Adapted material: the problem statements (rewritten), the input fixtures of the two
tests of each problem, and the reference transformations the Datapass references were
derived from. It reached Datapass through CodeDELeet's normalized import
(public/packs/v3-zilla.json, SHA-256 d3fd4f4cfc852b1056afc36c1e58b940a32ce22a810fa0a327d671b6bede7803; provenance ledger
docs/v3/ZILLA_IMPORT_PROVENANCE.json, SHA-256 97bb00ac7d408980ae088af5bef2ff4e2930314c0f475de1c6d44f60edbbbbe9). The private ZillaCode
archive was not used and the reference application was not run.

Modifications (see each exercise's "Source" section and provenance):
- statements rewritten for Datapass; table and column names normalized to snake_case;
- output contracts made explicit (column order, row order, NULL and tie rules), with
  documented corrections where the original statement and reference disagreed;
- references rewritten for DuckDB SQL, Snowflake SQL (translated to DuckDB), pandas,
  Polars, SparkLab and the Datapass dbt emulation;
- expected rows recomputed by running the Datapass references; hidden and edge
  fixtures added for ties, NULLs and empty groups.

The Datapass-authored parts of this pack are part of the Datapass Workbench repository.
